1
00:00:26,426 --> 00:00:27,127
They're all here?

2
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:28,530
Of course, they're all here.

3
00:00:28,563 --> 00:00:31,533
I told Naja Naja
I'd get 'em, didn't I?

4
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:38,472
Do they have
enough air in there, brother?

5
00:00:38,506 --> 00:00:40,875
Last time,
there wasn't enough air.

6
00:00:40,909 --> 00:00:43,477
Yeah, yeah.
You make one mistake...

7
00:00:43,511 --> 00:00:46,581
Don't worry.
They've got air, food, water.

8
00:00:46,648 --> 00:00:47,715
It's like a cruise ship.

9
00:00:47,749 --> 00:00:49,349
Hmm, good.

10
00:00:50,284 --> 00:00:52,185
We get this shipment
to the ceremony,

11
00:00:52,252 --> 00:00:55,055
our Lord might give you
another chance.

12
00:00:55,088 --> 00:00:58,626
Maybe you'll survive
in Kali Yuga's new world.

13
00:00:58,693 --> 00:00:59,861
You think so?

14
00:00:59,894 --> 00:01:01,029
Oh, man...

15
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,864
We'll get them there on time.
I promise, Chen.

16
00:01:02,931 --> 00:01:03,965
Kobra can count on me.

17
00:01:07,936 --> 00:01:09,938
Don't lose your head.
Back to back.

18
00:01:09,971 --> 00:01:12,072
Shoot at anything that moves.

19
00:01:12,574 --> 00:01:13,608
It's the bat.

20
00:01:13,675 --> 00:01:15,242
It's gotta be the bat!

21
00:01:22,115 --> 00:01:23,518
There!

22
00:01:33,895 --> 00:01:35,095
Did we get him?

23
00:01:35,195 --> 00:01:38,398
You cavort with demons
and call them gods!

24
00:01:39,934 --> 00:01:41,002
You embrace the darkness

25
00:01:41,069 --> 00:01:43,470
and treat it
as if it was light.

26
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:45,773
Your judgment is at hand.

27
00:01:46,908 --> 00:01:52,647
And I, Azrael...
find you guilty!

28
00:02:13,067 --> 00:02:15,135
What in the hell?

29
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:04,418
Which way?

30
00:03:04,451 --> 00:03:06,754
How should I know? Maybe--

31
00:03:18,866 --> 00:03:19,967
Defiler.

32
00:03:21,135 --> 00:03:22,335
Evil.

33
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:26,708
Your cult of serpents
must be punished.

34
00:03:26,774 --> 00:03:29,777
Please... please don't.

35
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:32,513
I promise. I'll change my ways.

36
00:03:33,114 --> 00:03:34,381
Please!

37
00:03:40,922 --> 00:03:43,524
Kali Yuga, thank you.

38
00:03:53,534 --> 00:03:55,235
Stay down.

39
00:05:06,974 --> 00:05:08,475
Someone call 911!

40
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:17,018
No... No, not this.

41
00:05:17,885 --> 00:05:19,319
Not again.

42
00:05:21,155 --> 00:05:22,790
Please.

43
00:05:22,824 --> 00:05:24,424
You have to help me.

44
00:05:25,193 --> 00:05:26,627
You have to.

45
00:07:11,532 --> 00:07:14,201
Come on. Push woman, push!

46
00:07:14,302 --> 00:07:15,569
That's it, that's it.

47
00:07:15,603 --> 00:07:17,939
C'mon, c'mon. Push!

48
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,590
Tell me.

49
00:07:36,624 --> 00:07:38,159
It's...

50
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,294
It's a boy.

51
00:07:40,361 --> 00:07:43,130
No, no!

52
00:07:43,631 --> 00:07:46,499
It can't be true. No, please!

53
00:07:47,935 --> 00:07:50,470
I'm so sorry,
my child.

54
00:07:51,038 --> 00:07:52,606
I'm sorry.

55
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:55,042
I'm sorry.

56
00:08:03,818 --> 00:08:05,953
Look, ma'am.

57
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:08,289
I do not make
the rules.

58
00:08:08,322 --> 00:08:09,957
This is our way.

59
00:08:09,991 --> 00:08:13,327
You and the boy must pay
for your husband's sins.

60
00:08:13,427 --> 00:08:15,196
It isn't right!

61
00:08:15,296 --> 00:08:18,532
Life rarely is.

62
00:08:37,785 --> 00:08:41,222
-Oh, now what do we have here?
-Huh?

63
00:08:44,325 --> 00:08:45,326
Hey!

64
00:08:47,595 --> 00:08:51,165
Right now, I'm gonna
have a little snack.

65
00:08:54,435 --> 00:08:56,170
What? Where is it?

66
00:08:57,671 --> 00:08:59,273
Oh, you think that's funny?

67
00:09:15,823 --> 00:09:16,490
Momma!

68
00:09:17,825 --> 00:09:18,959
Momma.

69
00:09:19,393 --> 00:09:21,228
Here, eat.

70
00:09:22,563 --> 00:09:25,232
What have I told you? Huh?

71
00:09:25,299 --> 00:09:27,835
No weakness. No pity.

72
00:09:29,203 --> 00:09:30,371
Even for me.

73
00:09:30,438 --> 00:09:33,207
You want to be kind
to your mama?

74
00:09:33,274 --> 00:09:35,743
Then survive. Dominate.

75
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:39,780
Subjugate!

76
00:09:39,814 --> 00:09:41,749
<i>- </i> But mom...
- No.

77
00:09:41,816 --> 00:09:45,486
You do not make me
strong by showing me mercy.

78
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,955
If I am to live,
I must want to.

79
00:09:47,988 --> 00:09:52,626
If you are to live,
you must want to.

80
00:09:55,229 --> 00:09:57,998
This is the way of the world.

81
00:10:20,387 --> 00:10:22,189
He's here.

82
00:10:28,362 --> 00:10:30,331
I found something for you.

83
00:10:31,332 --> 00:10:33,934
-What is it?
-An old magazine.

84
00:10:33,968 --> 00:10:36,737
But it talks about Gotham City.

85
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:40,040
A place
with the prettiest women...

86
00:10:40,542 --> 00:10:42,176
and handsome-looking men and

87
00:10:42,209 --> 00:10:46,180
skyscrapers as high
as the eye can see.

88
00:10:46,247 --> 00:10:50,151
It's a place a boy
could become a man.

89
00:10:50,251 --> 00:10:51,986
-Here.
-"Gotham Today.

90
00:10:52,052 --> 00:10:55,089
The strength
of Thomas Wayne..."

91
00:10:55,756 --> 00:10:58,192
Thank you.

92
00:10:58,225 --> 00:10:59,360
Of course.

93
00:11:00,427 --> 00:11:02,830
How is your mother?

94
00:11:03,931 --> 00:11:04,698
Sick.

95
00:11:04,732 --> 00:11:08,736
Oh... I am sorry.

96
00:11:08,769 --> 00:11:11,839
But if you need me,
I'll be here.

97
00:11:13,274 --> 00:11:16,310
Look, Momma.
I have something new to read.

98
00:11:18,245 --> 00:11:20,147
A wonder.

99
00:11:20,181 --> 00:11:23,184
I thought you have read
everything they have.

100
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:27,054
Why?

101
00:11:27,755 --> 00:11:29,423
Why do we read?

102
00:11:29,456 --> 00:11:31,725
Because knowledge is strength.

103
00:11:31,792 --> 00:11:34,929
And strength is survival.

104
00:11:35,496 --> 00:11:36,830
Yes.

105
00:11:37,364 --> 00:11:38,866
Good.

106
00:11:44,371 --> 00:11:45,839
What is it about?

107
00:11:45,873 --> 00:11:48,643
Someone named Thomas Wayne.

108
00:11:48,709 --> 00:11:50,444
He lives in Gotham City.

109
00:11:50,477 --> 00:11:52,279
I have heard of him.

110
00:11:52,813 --> 00:11:56,116
He is a powerful man.

111
00:11:57,351 --> 00:11:58,953
A strong man.

112
00:11:59,887 --> 00:12:01,789
You could be a man like him.

113
00:12:01,855 --> 00:12:05,259
Not from
inside these walls.

114
00:12:05,726 --> 00:12:09,396
Then grow.

115
00:12:10,130 --> 00:12:13,100
Grow until these walls
cannot hold you.

116
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:15,402
Till you burst free.

117
00:12:16,638 --> 00:12:18,839
Then you can show the world...

118
00:12:19,641 --> 00:12:22,510
people like this Thomas Wayne,

119
00:12:23,612 --> 00:12:26,180
what true strength is.

120
00:12:36,524 --> 00:12:37,726
I will, Momma.

121
00:12:37,791 --> 00:12:39,827
I'll make them bow before me.

122
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:43,097
And then, I'll give you
a palace in the sky.

123
00:12:43,163 --> 00:12:45,866
The world will know
our name, Momma.

124
00:12:45,966 --> 00:12:47,901
Someday,
we'll go to this Gotham,

125
00:12:47,935 --> 00:12:51,038
and it will be ours.

126
00:13:05,687 --> 00:13:06,820
Don't worry.

127
00:13:06,854 --> 00:13:10,224
Someday, it will be ours.

128
00:13:17,732 --> 00:13:19,099
Mmm...

129
00:13:19,933 --> 00:13:22,369
I heard about your mother.

130
00:13:23,904 --> 00:13:26,206
You're all alone now.

131
00:13:34,982 --> 00:13:37,752
Well, I know you must be sad,

132
00:13:37,818 --> 00:13:41,088
but I can comfort you.

133
00:13:42,056 --> 00:13:46,528
It's good to let others
carry your burdens.

134
00:13:47,762 --> 00:13:49,263
That is weakness!

135
00:13:49,330 --> 00:13:51,398
The strong carry
their own burdens.

136
00:13:51,432 --> 00:13:56,270
And the weak,
they deserve what they get.

137
00:14:03,110 --> 00:14:04,078
Hey!

138
00:14:08,349 --> 00:14:10,017
Calm down!

139
00:14:10,384 --> 00:14:11,385
Boy...

140
00:14:11,919 --> 00:14:13,555
what have you done?

141
00:14:20,562 --> 00:14:22,630
Goddamn it!

142
00:14:22,664 --> 00:14:24,632
That is not a boy.

143
00:14:24,666 --> 00:14:25,966
That's a demon.

144
00:14:25,999 --> 00:14:29,236
A bane
to everything that is holy.

145
00:14:29,838 --> 00:14:30,772
Take him.

146
00:14:30,805 --> 00:14:34,542
Place him
in the Cavidad Oscuro.

147
00:14:48,422 --> 00:14:53,227
It would be a mercy
to kill you quickly... Bane.

148
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:56,831
But there is
no more mercy here.

149
00:14:56,865 --> 00:15:01,068
The government forbids me
from executing you,

150
00:15:01,603 --> 00:15:03,671
but I have other ways.

151
00:15:05,807 --> 00:15:07,007
Don't worry.

152
00:15:07,074 --> 00:15:10,745
No one has survived
the Cavidad Oscuro for long.

153
00:15:11,846 --> 00:15:14,616
So your stay
will be a short one.

154
00:15:15,784 --> 00:15:16,851
Here's something for you

155
00:15:16,917 --> 00:15:19,953
to pass what little time
you have left.

156
00:15:37,705 --> 00:15:40,575
- Ah, look at that.
- You have friends!

157
00:15:40,642 --> 00:15:43,511
<i>Hiciste amigos.</i>

158
00:15:45,145 --> 00:15:49,884
I see the hate burning
in your eyes, boy.

159
00:15:49,983 --> 00:15:53,253
Let's hope it's enough
to keep you warm.

160
00:17:42,095 --> 00:17:43,965
Is that the kid?

161
00:17:43,998 --> 00:17:46,266
How long has he been
down there?

162
00:17:46,333 --> 00:17:47,802
Forever.

163
00:17:47,835 --> 00:17:51,371
If he can survive, so can we.

164
00:17:52,574 --> 00:17:54,609
He has shown us.

165
00:18:06,286 --> 00:18:10,525
You are a survivor,
which means you are strong.

166
00:18:11,025 --> 00:18:13,928
And we need strong men.

167
00:18:13,962 --> 00:18:17,464
Our government
has created something.

168
00:18:17,532 --> 00:18:21,401
Something that will
make our soldiers more than...

169
00:18:22,402 --> 00:18:24,271
mortal.

170
00:18:24,304 --> 00:18:29,409
If we can find someone
strong enough to withstand it.

171
00:18:29,443 --> 00:18:32,212
We've had little
success so far.

172
00:18:32,245 --> 00:18:35,248
But maybe you
will be different, eh?

173
00:18:35,282 --> 00:18:40,487
This is your chance to pay
for the sins of your father.

174
00:18:44,124 --> 00:18:46,393
It is called "Venom."

175
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,427
And with it,

176
00:18:47,494 --> 00:18:52,000
we will return Santa Prisca
to its former glory.

177
00:19:03,711 --> 00:19:05,913
Our glory.

178
00:19:17,091 --> 00:19:18,660
Ah...

179
00:19:18,693 --> 00:19:20,260
I thought
he would survive

180
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:22,462
where the others could not.

181
00:19:23,131 --> 00:19:24,297
No matter.

182
00:19:24,364 --> 00:19:27,735
I have an entire building
of unwilling guinea pigs.

183
00:20:25,893 --> 00:20:27,762
No, no!

184
00:20:34,001 --> 00:20:36,671
Please... don't...

185
00:20:47,115 --> 00:20:50,551
Please, I...
I'll give you anything.

186
00:20:50,651 --> 00:20:51,986
Just let me live.

187
00:20:53,755 --> 00:20:55,590
Live?

188
00:20:55,656 --> 00:21:03,330
You do not know what it means
to live. It is not a right.

189
00:21:03,363 --> 00:21:05,767
It is a prize...

190
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:08,703
A prize which must be won!

191
00:21:08,770 --> 00:21:10,738
Please.

192
00:21:10,772 --> 00:21:13,273
I should thank you.

193
00:21:13,306 --> 00:21:15,510
You made me survive.

194
00:21:15,576 --> 00:21:18,980
Made me embrace the darkness.

195
00:21:19,046 --> 00:21:21,082
Learn what true strength is.

196
00:21:21,149 --> 00:21:24,719
And now I must give
others that gift.

197
00:21:25,119 --> 00:21:26,087
What...

198
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,121
What...

199
00:21:27,188 --> 00:21:28,288
What are you?

200
00:21:28,355 --> 00:21:34,095
What you said,
"a demon, an abomination.

201
00:21:34,128 --> 00:21:39,967
A bane to everything
that is holy."

202
00:21:46,741 --> 00:21:47,842
Surrender!

203
00:21:49,977 --> 00:21:50,945
No.

204
00:21:51,012 --> 00:21:52,345
No, <i>por favor...</i> No!

205
00:22:04,091 --> 00:22:08,461
Bane!
Bane! Bane! Bane! Bane!

206
00:22:20,708 --> 00:22:24,212
So,
what gives you hope, Mr. Wayne?

207
00:22:24,245 --> 00:22:25,546
Now?

208
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,115
Well, I hope
we can move this along

209
00:22:28,182 --> 00:22:29,449
so I can go back to work.

210
00:22:29,517 --> 00:22:31,152
Please take this seriously.

211
00:22:31,185 --> 00:22:32,286
Oh, I am.

212
00:22:32,385 --> 00:22:33,754
I thought you were
supposed to help me

213
00:22:33,821 --> 00:22:35,890
with some of my
more serious physical problems.

214
00:22:35,957 --> 00:22:39,160
In order to do what I do,
to heal the body,

215
00:22:39,227 --> 00:22:41,762
we have to make sure
we heal the mind.

216
00:22:41,796 --> 00:22:47,367
So, as I was saying,
what gives you hope?

217
00:22:47,869 --> 00:22:49,036
I don't know.

218
00:22:49,070 --> 00:22:50,338
A good scotch.

219
00:22:50,403 --> 00:22:51,639
A nice watch.

220
00:22:51,672 --> 00:22:53,574
Uh-huh.

221
00:22:53,641 --> 00:22:55,743
If you won't start,
maybe I should.

222
00:22:55,810 --> 00:22:58,378
Mr. Wayne, I did a deep dive
on you the other day.

223
00:22:58,411 --> 00:23:00,548
-I'm flattered.
-Don't be.

224
00:23:00,581 --> 00:23:02,984
What I found
was really quite interesting.

225
00:23:03,017 --> 00:23:05,353
The tabloids reported
you had a falling out

226
00:23:05,418 --> 00:23:07,655
with your son, Dick Grayson?

227
00:23:09,023 --> 00:23:10,558
<i>It was...</i>

228
00:23:11,559 --> 00:23:14,262
<i>It was time for him to move on.</i>

229
00:23:14,295 --> 00:23:18,332
And then your second ward,
Jason Todd?

230
00:23:18,366 --> 00:23:21,468
By your own admission,
a hard case.

231
00:23:21,502 --> 00:23:24,772
<i>Well...</i>
<i>I'm sorry for your loss.</i>

232
00:23:28,342 --> 00:23:31,846
And you mentioned
a new intern at work. Tim?

233
00:23:31,913 --> 00:23:33,147
He's... um...

234
00:23:33,180 --> 00:23:35,816
<i>Smart. Determined.</i>

235
00:23:36,651 --> 00:23:38,119
-In need?
-I'm sorry.

236
00:23:38,185 --> 00:23:39,854
I don't really understand--

237
00:23:39,921 --> 00:23:41,055
Oh, Mr. Wayne.

238
00:23:42,189 --> 00:23:43,824
Bruce, please.

239
00:23:43,891 --> 00:23:48,162
Mr. Wayne,
we both know you understand.

240
00:23:48,229 --> 00:23:49,697
You may have all of your board,

241
00:23:49,730 --> 00:23:50,898
the media, whatever debutante

242
00:23:50,932 --> 00:23:52,767
you take out
on the town fooled.

243
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:55,468
But I've been listening to you
for a few days,

244
00:23:55,503 --> 00:23:58,506
and I know
how intelligent you are.

245
00:23:58,572 --> 00:24:02,243
I know the mask you put on
for those around you.

246
00:24:02,276 --> 00:24:05,746
I'm here because I thought
you might be able to help me

247
00:24:05,780 --> 00:24:07,915
with some of my
physical issues.

248
00:24:07,949 --> 00:24:11,652
No. You're here because
your surrogate father

249
00:24:11,719 --> 00:24:14,555
said he'd quit
if you didn't find help.

250
00:24:14,622 --> 00:24:17,725
I want to help you, Mr. Wayne.

251
00:24:17,758 --> 00:24:19,760
And in order for me to help,

252
00:24:19,794 --> 00:24:22,630
I need to know
what and who I'm helping.

253
00:24:23,397 --> 00:24:24,699
I see.

254
00:24:24,765 --> 00:24:27,268
I'll make sure you're paid
for wasting your time.

255
00:24:27,335 --> 00:24:29,603
When I ask you
what gives you hope,

256
00:24:29,637 --> 00:24:32,974
it seems obvious to me.
But you don't seem to see it.

257
00:24:33,841 --> 00:24:34,976
Enlighten me.

258
00:24:35,042 --> 00:24:38,478
People. Helping people.

259
00:24:38,512 --> 00:24:40,982
It's obvious from your own
personal tragedies

260
00:24:41,048 --> 00:24:43,517
that you're working out
the trauma you experienced

261
00:24:43,617 --> 00:24:46,053
as a little boy
by helping others.

262
00:24:46,087 --> 00:24:47,822
What's fascinating, however,

263
00:24:47,888 --> 00:24:50,257
is that you don't
recognize the need

264
00:24:50,324 --> 00:24:51,592
to be helped in return.

265
00:24:51,659 --> 00:24:53,361
Instead, you continue to think

266
00:24:53,394 --> 00:24:55,429
these people would be lost
without you.

267
00:24:55,463 --> 00:24:57,631
Which makes you,
if I can be blunt...

268
00:24:57,665 --> 00:24:59,000
You weren't before?

269
00:24:59,033 --> 00:25:02,169
It makes you a control freak
with a messiah complex.

270
00:25:02,603 --> 00:25:04,038
You need help, Mr. Wayne.

271
00:25:04,071 --> 00:25:07,441
And if you don't ask for it,
something's going to break.

272
00:25:07,508 --> 00:25:08,542
And things that break

273
00:25:08,609 --> 00:25:11,078
aren't easily
put back together.

274
00:25:20,021 --> 00:25:22,256
Cell 113, secured.

275
00:25:22,289 --> 00:25:24,392
Cell 114, secured.

276
00:25:24,425 --> 00:25:25,693
Secure?

277
00:25:25,726 --> 00:25:28,796
If I was secure,
I'm sure they'd let me out.

278
00:25:28,829 --> 00:25:33,367
I am late for a tea party,
after all.

279
00:25:33,401 --> 00:25:35,936
Nutball.

280
00:25:43,344 --> 00:25:44,513
Stan?

281
00:25:44,545 --> 00:25:46,847
I just heard a noise
in the east wing.

282
00:25:46,914 --> 00:25:48,549
Is that you?

283
00:25:49,216 --> 00:25:50,718
Stan?

284
00:25:51,786 --> 00:25:54,288
Stan, this isn't funny.

285
00:25:54,321 --> 00:25:55,489
Ohh...

286
00:25:55,524 --> 00:25:57,992
Well, maybe
you're going bonkers.

287
00:25:58,025 --> 00:26:00,461
But I'll tell you
a little secret,

288
00:26:00,529 --> 00:26:04,732
all the best people are.

289
00:26:05,332 --> 00:26:07,468
Shut up, Hatter!

290
00:26:07,501 --> 00:26:08,537
Stan!

291
00:26:08,602 --> 00:26:10,371
Okay, I'm pulling the alarm.

292
00:26:10,438 --> 00:26:11,472
You hear me?

293
00:26:13,574 --> 00:26:14,875
I hear you.

294
00:26:22,616 --> 00:26:23,784
Ohh...

295
00:26:23,851 --> 00:26:26,454
I might make the tea party
after all.

296
00:26:26,521 --> 00:26:28,189
<i>♪ I'm going to the party ♪</i>

297
00:26:28,222 --> 00:26:30,257
<i>♪ I'm going to the party ♪</i>

298
00:26:46,807 --> 00:26:50,044
The liberation
of Gotham begins.

299
00:27:10,764 --> 00:27:12,500
Shouldn't you slow down?

300
00:27:12,567 --> 00:27:13,801
No.

301
00:27:15,903 --> 00:27:17,638
I didn't mean driving.

302
00:27:18,072 --> 00:27:19,140
I meant...

303
00:27:19,173 --> 00:27:22,611
You haven't slept since Arkham
exploded two days ago.

304
00:27:22,710 --> 00:27:24,011
You need to rest.

305
00:27:24,044 --> 00:27:26,480
I'll rest when everyone
that's escaped is captured.

306
00:27:26,548 --> 00:27:28,015
Not before.

307
00:27:29,150 --> 00:27:30,718
Right now,
we're all that stands

308
00:27:30,751 --> 00:27:32,987
between those inmates
and the fall of Gotham.

309
00:27:33,020 --> 00:27:35,356
Well, maybe we should ask
Jean-Paul for help.

310
00:27:35,422 --> 00:27:36,625
His training is coming along

311
00:27:36,657 --> 00:27:38,292
and he hasn't
had an outburst in--

312
00:27:38,325 --> 00:27:41,996
I told you, he's a bomb
that needs to be defused.

313
00:27:42,096 --> 00:27:43,632
The only reason
he's in the cave is that

314
00:27:43,697 --> 00:27:47,001
we have a chance to help him
where no one else would.

315
00:27:47,067 --> 00:27:48,969
We just need to keep
an eye on him,

316
00:27:49,003 --> 00:27:51,872
to give him purpose,
to show him his skills

317
00:27:51,939 --> 00:27:54,375
can be a blessing
instead of a curse.

318
00:27:54,708 --> 00:27:55,976
We're here.

319
00:28:02,716 --> 00:28:03,518
Stay put.

320
00:28:03,552 --> 00:28:05,520
What? I'm coming with you.

321
00:28:05,554 --> 00:28:06,921
No, you're not.

322
00:28:06,987 --> 00:28:11,392
Man the aerial drone. Relay
anything that might warrant it.

323
00:28:13,662 --> 00:28:14,995
Yes, sir.

324
00:28:26,273 --> 00:28:27,241
North of your location,

325
00:28:27,308 --> 00:28:30,477
it looks like Mad Hatter
is having a party.

326
00:28:31,712 --> 00:28:36,217
Yes, yes.
You're all doing splendidly.

327
00:28:36,250 --> 00:28:40,054
Now, I think it's time
for dessert.

328
00:28:40,087 --> 00:28:44,391
Everyone, you see
the knives in front of you?

329
00:28:44,425 --> 00:28:46,260
Pick them up.

330
00:28:50,632 --> 00:28:54,068
You all had a hand
in sending me to Arkham.

331
00:28:54,101 --> 00:28:59,206
So why not use those hands
to kill yourselves?

332
00:29:09,883 --> 00:29:12,554
Oh, look, it's Batman.

333
00:29:12,621 --> 00:29:13,622
Hello, dear.

334
00:29:13,655 --> 00:29:15,222
How nice of you to join us.

335
00:29:15,256 --> 00:29:17,024
Come on, sit down.

336
00:29:17,057 --> 00:29:17,925
Sit down.

337
00:29:17,958 --> 00:29:19,728
Would you like
a nice cup of tea?

338
00:29:19,793 --> 00:29:22,997
Mad Hatter, the party's over.

339
00:29:23,030 --> 00:29:24,365
Over?

340
00:29:24,465 --> 00:29:27,034
But, we just got here.

341
00:29:27,101 --> 00:29:29,837
My friends are wearing
their party hats,

342
00:29:29,870 --> 00:29:33,874
and now they'll do
whatever I want them to do.

343
00:29:33,941 --> 00:29:35,710
And what I want them to do,

344
00:29:35,744 --> 00:29:39,046
is play a favorite game
of a friend of mine.

345
00:29:39,079 --> 00:29:41,181
Off with your head.
Off with your head.

346
00:29:41,248 --> 00:29:43,518
Off with your head.
Off with your head.

347
00:29:43,551 --> 00:29:45,786
Off with your head!

348
00:29:57,831 --> 00:29:58,866
Oh!

349
00:29:58,932 --> 00:30:01,869
My days!
I've never seen that before.

350
00:30:01,902 --> 00:30:06,073
Well, Batman,
you've really lost your touch.

351
00:30:06,106 --> 00:30:08,809
I expected more
from the Dark Knight.

352
00:30:17,418 --> 00:30:19,521
What? Where am I?

353
00:30:33,735 --> 00:30:36,738
This party is getting boring.

354
00:30:36,771 --> 00:30:39,840
Let's end the night
with a bang!

355
00:30:46,413 --> 00:30:48,882
You insolent--

356
00:30:51,753 --> 00:30:53,153
I told you to wait in the car.

357
00:30:53,187 --> 00:30:57,424
I'm sorry. I... It looked like
you needed some help.

358
00:31:01,763 --> 00:31:03,030
Hmm.

359
00:31:20,749 --> 00:31:23,384
- No!
- Jean-Paul?

360
00:31:23,785 --> 00:31:25,119
Are you all right?

361
00:31:26,521 --> 00:31:27,856
Alfred.

362
00:31:29,824 --> 00:31:31,058
Yes.

363
00:31:31,925 --> 00:31:33,193
Yes, I think so.

364
00:31:33,628 --> 00:31:34,361
Take heart.

365
00:31:34,395 --> 00:31:36,930
You lasted longer
than last time,

366
00:31:36,997 --> 00:31:39,032
and the time before that.

367
00:31:39,066 --> 00:31:41,736
All in all, you're making
tremendous progress.

368
00:31:41,803 --> 00:31:43,203
Yes, but...

369
00:31:44,371 --> 00:31:47,274
Uh, what they did to me,
Alfred.

370
00:31:48,075 --> 00:31:51,345
I had a life before Azrael.

371
00:31:52,012 --> 00:31:54,081
Before the Order of Dumas.

372
00:31:55,449 --> 00:31:57,084
At least I thought I did.

373
00:31:58,185 --> 00:31:59,554
Now I...

374
00:31:59,621 --> 00:32:02,690
I don't know who or...

375
00:32:03,625 --> 00:32:04,626
what I am.

376
00:32:04,692 --> 00:32:07,729
You are a man that was abused

377
00:32:07,796 --> 00:32:12,867
by this Order of Dumas...
Your father.

378
00:32:12,933 --> 00:32:15,469
What they did
was unconscionable.

379
00:32:16,638 --> 00:32:17,772
But we'll fix it, my boy.

380
00:32:17,806 --> 00:32:22,276
Batman does not take people
into his confidence lightly.

381
00:32:22,309 --> 00:32:24,945
You're here because he thinks
it's the best place

382
00:32:24,978 --> 00:32:27,615
for you to heal, to recover.

383
00:32:28,583 --> 00:32:30,017
And you're well on your way.

384
00:32:30,083 --> 00:32:33,053
In the meantime,
may I recommend doing

385
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:36,624
what we Englishmen do
when things get a bit rough?

386
00:32:37,424 --> 00:32:38,693
What's that?

387
00:32:38,726 --> 00:32:40,227
Have a spot of tea.

388
00:32:48,903 --> 00:32:50,572
I was not trying
to disobey you.

389
00:32:50,605 --> 00:32:54,041
I just... It looked like
you needed help, that's all.

390
00:32:54,141 --> 00:32:56,911
What I need is for you
to follow orders.

391
00:32:56,945 --> 00:32:59,514
Look into what caused
the explosion at Arkham.

392
00:32:59,547 --> 00:33:00,615
Ask Jean-Paul.

393
00:33:00,648 --> 00:33:02,951
Maybe his considerable
computer skills can be of use.

394
00:33:03,016 --> 00:33:05,385
I should be in the field and--

395
00:33:06,019 --> 00:33:08,355
Right. Understood.

396
00:33:08,388 --> 00:33:11,860
Master Bruce,
may I make you some food, sir?

397
00:33:11,926 --> 00:33:14,261
No, Alfred,
I'm just back to resupply.

398
00:33:14,328 --> 00:33:19,601
Sir, if I may,
you are looking a bit weary.

399
00:33:19,634 --> 00:33:20,568
You need to sleep.

400
00:33:20,602 --> 00:33:23,571
I'm sure the Arkham escapees
would love that,

401
00:33:23,638 --> 00:33:25,372
but I can't give them a break.

402
00:33:25,405 --> 00:33:26,139
Not now.

403
00:33:26,173 --> 00:33:28,710
Radio in if you find anything.

404
00:33:30,512 --> 00:33:32,112
He's tired, Tim.

405
00:33:32,179 --> 00:33:35,683
I'm sure you'll be back out
on patrol in no time.

406
00:33:35,717 --> 00:33:37,384
I know.

407
00:33:37,752 --> 00:33:39,152
I'm just worried.

408
00:33:39,219 --> 00:33:42,322
He's been going nonstop
for two days.

409
00:33:42,356 --> 00:33:44,792
That's a long time
with no rest,

410
00:33:45,660 --> 00:33:46,594
even for Batman.

411
00:33:46,661 --> 00:33:48,930
Yes, you're right, of course.

412
00:33:48,963 --> 00:33:51,533
Since you'll be staying here
for the evening,

413
00:33:51,599 --> 00:33:54,669
shall I tell your father
that you'll be working late?

414
00:33:54,736 --> 00:33:56,004
I'm not staying here.

415
00:33:56,036 --> 00:33:58,873
Master Bruce wanted you
to stay in the Batcave.

416
00:33:58,907 --> 00:34:02,042
He didn't say stay
in the Batcave.

417
00:34:02,109 --> 00:34:04,177
He said, "Figure out
how Arkham exploded

418
00:34:04,211 --> 00:34:07,314
with Jean-Paul." And that's
exactly what we're gonna do.

419
00:34:07,381 --> 00:34:10,117
I don't think Master Bruce
will take kindly

420
00:34:10,150 --> 00:34:12,185
to your semantic loophole.

421
00:34:12,252 --> 00:34:14,488
If Batman's gonna
push himself to the edge,

422
00:34:14,522 --> 00:34:16,958
I have to try to help him
as best I can.

423
00:34:16,991 --> 00:34:18,927
I need to check out
the bomb site in person.

424
00:34:18,960 --> 00:34:21,596
I'll be careful, I promise.

425
00:34:22,496 --> 00:34:24,732
And Jean-Paul?

426
00:34:24,766 --> 00:34:26,568
Does he really need to go?

427
00:34:26,634 --> 00:34:29,971
He's been stuck in here
for weeks. Batman said,

428
00:34:30,004 --> 00:34:32,072
"We have to show him
there's more he can do."

429
00:34:32,139 --> 00:34:34,943
Besides, I don't have
a driver's license

430
00:34:35,043 --> 00:34:37,110
and I kinda need a lift.

431
00:34:47,387 --> 00:34:48,790
Zsasz is a killer.

432
00:34:48,823 --> 00:34:51,391
Every minute we are out here
puts those women in danger.

433
00:34:51,458 --> 00:34:56,196
I'm not sending my men in there
to be killed one at a time.

434
00:34:56,496 --> 00:34:57,431
We wait.

435
00:34:57,464 --> 00:35:00,267
For what? Your vigilante friend
to show up?

436
00:35:02,402 --> 00:35:05,540
I'll, uh, check on SWAT's ETA.

437
00:35:06,206 --> 00:35:07,207
Commissioner,

438
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:09,209
we are paid to stand
in harm's way.

439
00:35:09,242 --> 00:35:10,545
That's the job.

440
00:35:10,578 --> 00:35:13,948
Some day, he won't be here
to clean up our city's mess,

441
00:35:13,982 --> 00:35:16,416
and it's gonna be up to us.

442
00:35:16,884 --> 00:35:17,986
We know what to do.

443
00:35:18,019 --> 00:35:19,921
Just let us do it.

444
00:35:19,954 --> 00:35:24,626
There's a difference between
what we do and what he does.

445
00:35:25,292 --> 00:35:26,594
If that day comes,

446
00:35:26,628 --> 00:35:29,429
the one you're describing,
Detective Montoya,

447
00:35:29,463 --> 00:35:32,299
where he's not here to fight
these crazies,

448
00:35:32,399 --> 00:35:34,902
Gotham City
will already be lost.

449
00:35:34,936 --> 00:35:38,573
And there won't be a damn thing
we can do about it.

450
00:35:40,975 --> 00:35:42,710
I'll check the perimeter.

451
00:35:47,882 --> 00:35:49,316
Don't prove me wrong.

452
00:36:26,386 --> 00:36:30,190
Please, no! Please, no!

453
00:36:30,223 --> 00:36:32,359
-Please.
-Come here, zombie.

454
00:36:32,392 --> 00:36:35,362
Let my blade
have a look at you.

455
00:36:36,164 --> 00:36:37,699
Please. Please don't.

456
00:36:37,732 --> 00:36:41,401
You spend so much time
on your face,

457
00:36:41,435 --> 00:36:46,206
your hair, your makeup.
It's all so pointless.

458
00:36:46,239 --> 00:36:50,343
Your existence is pointless.

459
00:36:50,377 --> 00:36:52,513
Just another zombie.

460
00:36:52,580 --> 00:36:53,581
But I'm here,

461
00:36:53,648 --> 00:36:58,019
here to set you free
from your meaningless life!

462
00:36:58,086 --> 00:36:59,754
Isn't that wonderful?

463
00:37:03,057 --> 00:37:03,858
Freeze!

464
00:37:03,891 --> 00:37:06,961
Put the gun down, zombie,

465
00:37:06,994 --> 00:37:08,730
or this pretty smile

466
00:37:08,796 --> 00:37:10,998
gets a whole lot wider.

467
00:37:11,065 --> 00:37:12,499
Let the girl go, Zsasz!

468
00:37:12,533 --> 00:37:15,402
Why? So she can keep doing
the same things over and over?

469
00:37:15,469 --> 00:37:18,940
Not gonna happen, zombie.

470
00:37:24,779 --> 00:37:26,346
Take me.

471
00:37:26,748 --> 00:37:28,281
Take me instead.

472
00:37:29,751 --> 00:37:30,918
A hero?

473
00:37:31,686 --> 00:37:33,054
How sweet.

474
00:37:33,487 --> 00:37:34,889
The gun's down.

475
00:37:35,857 --> 00:37:36,891
I'm right here.

476
00:37:36,958 --> 00:37:40,862
Well, I'm sure
you'll taste sweet too.

477
00:37:40,895 --> 00:37:43,296
All that blue blood.

478
00:37:47,735 --> 00:37:50,138
What did your sacrifice
get you?

479
00:37:50,204 --> 00:37:51,304
Hmm?

480
00:37:51,338 --> 00:37:54,441
After you're dead,
I'll move on to the rest,

481
00:37:54,509 --> 00:37:56,978
and nothing on this earth

482
00:37:57,645 --> 00:37:58,946
can stop me.

483
00:38:04,284 --> 00:38:06,486
Oh, look at him, zombie.

484
00:38:06,521 --> 00:38:08,890
You can see it, can't you?

485
00:38:08,923 --> 00:38:10,725
He's just like me.

486
00:38:10,792 --> 00:38:11,759
A predator.

487
00:38:11,793 --> 00:38:13,261
He's not like you.

488
00:38:13,326 --> 00:38:14,595
He doesn't kill.

489
00:38:14,662 --> 00:38:16,030
He doesn't?

490
00:38:16,063 --> 00:38:17,832
How can you be sure?

491
00:38:18,331 --> 00:38:20,168
Oh, look at him...

492
00:38:20,201 --> 00:38:23,370
tired, wavering...

493
00:38:23,403 --> 00:38:30,144
How long before he gives in
to his darker desires?

494
00:38:30,211 --> 00:38:32,713
Oh, come on, let's find out.

495
00:38:33,815 --> 00:38:35,650
What do you say?

496
00:38:35,716 --> 00:38:37,051
I say...

497
00:38:37,084 --> 00:38:38,553
you talk too much.

498
00:38:42,455 --> 00:38:43,925
You have the hostages?

499
00:38:43,958 --> 00:38:45,026
Go!

500
00:39:15,857 --> 00:39:17,357
Predator...

501
00:39:17,625 --> 00:39:19,260
like me.

502
00:39:38,411 --> 00:39:40,514
Batman! Stop!

503
00:39:44,051 --> 00:39:44,952
I...

504
00:39:45,019 --> 00:39:46,687
Is he dead?

505
00:39:48,589 --> 00:39:53,761
Just... like... me.

506
00:39:53,794 --> 00:39:55,830
No.

507
00:39:56,097 --> 00:39:58,099
I... I...

508
00:39:58,165 --> 00:39:59,567
I need to go.

509
00:40:03,403 --> 00:40:04,805
You almost killed him.

510
00:40:04,839 --> 00:40:08,943
If this is how you help,
you're no better than they are.

511
00:40:14,882 --> 00:40:17,218
What the hell happened,
Montoya?

512
00:40:17,285 --> 00:40:19,687
Your hero, Commissioner,

513
00:40:20,321 --> 00:40:21,856
he's losing control.

514
00:40:33,768 --> 00:40:35,569
Are you sure
I need to wear this?

515
00:40:35,603 --> 00:40:39,006
Can't have anyone linking you
to me or Batman, you know?

516
00:40:48,916 --> 00:40:51,385
What exactly
are we looking for?

517
00:40:51,419 --> 00:40:52,753
Evidence.

518
00:40:54,655 --> 00:40:57,558
Reports said that
it was a gas explosion.

519
00:40:57,591 --> 00:41:00,261
But GCPD, fire,

520
00:41:00,328 --> 00:41:01,996
everyone seems to be
stretched thin.

521
00:41:02,029 --> 00:41:03,998
I'm guessing they barely
looked this place over

522
00:41:04,065 --> 00:41:06,434
before they headed
to their next emergency.

523
00:41:16,310 --> 00:41:19,180
Hey, Robin, what's this?

524
00:41:22,516 --> 00:41:24,051
Huh.

525
00:41:24,085 --> 00:41:25,086
That's unusual.

526
00:41:25,152 --> 00:41:26,087
What is?

527
00:41:26,187 --> 00:41:27,455
The burn pattern here.

528
00:41:27,521 --> 00:41:31,625
Or the lack of one.
Like something exploded out.

529
00:41:31,692 --> 00:41:34,261
Look, see the scorch marks
moving upward

530
00:41:34,328 --> 00:41:36,163
almost in a sphere shape.

531
00:41:36,197 --> 00:41:37,798
This was a bomb.

532
00:41:37,832 --> 00:41:40,334
Some sort of
multiple plastique.

533
00:41:40,434 --> 00:41:42,236
How do you know all this stuff?

534
00:41:42,269 --> 00:41:43,437
You're just a kid.

535
00:41:43,504 --> 00:41:45,840
A kid that loves
mysteries, puzzles.

536
00:41:45,873 --> 00:41:48,009
I may never be the detective
that Batman is,

537
00:41:48,109 --> 00:41:51,746
but I'm definitely gonna
give him a run for his money.

538
00:41:54,148 --> 00:41:56,117
Here. Look.

539
00:41:56,217 --> 00:41:57,685
There's the detonator.

540
00:41:59,387 --> 00:42:01,889
A little of
the explosive residue.

541
00:42:01,922 --> 00:42:02,556
And...

542
00:42:02,656 --> 00:42:03,858
That's a spectrometer.

543
00:42:03,924 --> 00:42:08,529
Yes, a very expensive
portable one.

544
00:42:08,562 --> 00:42:10,031
Hey, looks like you haven't

545
00:42:10,064 --> 00:42:11,832
forgotten everything
from your past.

546
00:42:11,866 --> 00:42:14,969
It's all jumbled,
like a puzzle.

547
00:42:15,002 --> 00:42:17,605
Bits and pieces
that come and go.

548
00:42:17,671 --> 00:42:19,573
I know, but don't worry,

549
00:42:19,607 --> 00:42:21,942
it will all come back,
I promise.

550
00:42:22,009 --> 00:42:25,346
But until then,
I appreciate your help.

551
00:42:25,413 --> 00:42:27,114
Well, beats midterms.

552
00:42:30,317 --> 00:42:33,821
I've seen this particular
brand of explosive before.

553
00:42:33,921 --> 00:42:37,091
A couple weeks ago, a member
of the Bertinelli crime family

554
00:42:37,158 --> 00:42:40,294
used it on an armored car,
which means...

555
00:42:40,327 --> 00:42:41,929
Another field trip?

556
00:42:41,962 --> 00:42:43,664
You read my mind.

557
00:42:56,610 --> 00:42:58,813
It's been
a couple of days, boss.

558
00:42:58,879 --> 00:43:02,216
You must've worked up a riddle
that'll get us rich.

559
00:43:02,283 --> 00:43:04,185
Riddle me this, boys.

560
00:43:04,218 --> 00:43:08,255
Why was the loud hunter
mauled by his prey?

561
00:43:08,823 --> 00:43:09,957
Hmm?

562
00:43:10,925 --> 00:43:13,294
Because he didn't
shut his trap.

563
00:43:14,361 --> 00:43:15,930
No.

564
00:43:15,996 --> 00:43:18,533
Something else
is going on out there.

565
00:43:18,632 --> 00:43:21,769
A riddle I haven't
found the answer to.

566
00:43:22,436 --> 00:43:25,272
We wait it out until the time--

567
00:43:27,842 --> 00:43:30,377
No one sits out tonight.

568
00:43:30,411 --> 00:43:31,879
Who...

569
00:43:32,379 --> 00:43:33,714
You.

570
00:43:33,781 --> 00:43:37,451
You are responsible
for all the chaos in Gotham.

571
00:43:37,485 --> 00:43:40,754
The chaos
has always been there.

572
00:43:40,821 --> 00:43:45,292
I'm just helping
everyone rise above it.

573
00:43:45,326 --> 00:43:46,293
And you...

574
00:43:46,327 --> 00:43:52,601
I am helping you find out
what true strength is.

575
00:44:05,212 --> 00:44:06,947
Scarface! No!

576
00:44:09,483 --> 00:44:11,620
You're losing it, Bats.

577
00:44:11,719 --> 00:44:14,155
Really losing it.

578
00:44:47,988 --> 00:44:51,125
I got him.
I got the Batman.

579
00:45:36,504 --> 00:45:38,607
Batman doesn't look so good.

580
00:45:38,673 --> 00:45:40,174
No.

581
00:45:40,274 --> 00:45:41,442
No, he doesn't.

582
00:45:53,220 --> 00:45:56,457
<i>Failed me.</i>
<i>You failed me. You failed me.</i>

583
00:45:57,659 --> 00:45:59,927
You got me killed.

584
00:46:00,427 --> 00:46:01,362
No.

585
00:46:01,395 --> 00:46:03,364
You're gonna get Tim killed.

586
00:46:03,397 --> 00:46:05,533
Jean-Paul, Alfred.

587
00:46:06,834 --> 00:46:09,671
This city would be
better off without you.

588
00:46:09,704 --> 00:46:12,439
You're the reason
Gotham suffers!

589
00:46:15,376 --> 00:46:18,379
This... isn't... real.

590
00:46:46,741 --> 00:46:47,808
<i>Hello?</i>

591
00:46:47,841 --> 00:46:49,443
<i>Hello?</i>

592
00:46:49,476 --> 00:46:51,345
<i>Is anyone there?</i>

593
00:46:51,812 --> 00:46:53,213
<i>Mr. Wayne?</i>

594
00:46:54,181 --> 00:46:55,382
<i>Bruce.</i>

595
00:46:55,449 --> 00:46:57,084
<i>Is that you?</i>

596
00:46:57,851 --> 00:47:00,020
I'm tired, Shondra.

597
00:47:00,054 --> 00:47:01,756
<i>Have you slept?</i>

598
00:47:01,790 --> 00:47:03,123
There's no time.

599
00:47:03,157 --> 00:47:05,492
<i>No time for what?</i>

600
00:47:05,527 --> 00:47:06,994
<i>Bruce...</i>

601
00:47:07,027 --> 00:47:09,531
<i>I want to help you,</i>
<i>but the first step</i>

602
00:47:09,597 --> 00:47:12,701
<i>in getting help is to want it.</i>

603
00:47:12,734 --> 00:47:14,835
<i>You called me for a reason.</i>

604
00:47:14,868 --> 00:47:16,937
<i>I know your work is important.</i>

605
00:47:17,004 --> 00:47:19,073
<i>I know that you've been</i>
<i>running yourself ragged.</i>

606
00:47:19,106 --> 00:47:22,677
<i>But, Bruce,</i>
<i>you need to slow down.</i>

607
00:47:22,711 --> 00:47:24,244
<i>Where are you?</i>

608
00:47:24,278 --> 00:47:25,245
In my car.

609
00:47:25,312 --> 00:47:26,880
<i>Good.</i>
<i>Come to the office.</i>

610
00:47:26,947 --> 00:47:29,116
<i>I'm working late anyway,</i>
<i>and we can talk.</i>

611
00:47:30,250 --> 00:47:31,285
Yeah.

612
00:47:31,885 --> 00:47:33,287
Yeah, I think I...

613
00:47:40,361 --> 00:47:41,328
I have to go.

614
00:47:41,395 --> 00:47:43,565
<i>Bruce, don't--</i>

615
00:48:23,303 --> 00:48:25,272
You figured it out!

616
00:48:25,305 --> 00:48:27,709
"I am a king that works
every day,

617
00:48:27,742 --> 00:48:33,347
every second, every hour,
every minute, day in day out."

618
00:48:34,948 --> 00:48:36,450
"What am I?"

619
00:48:36,518 --> 00:48:40,220
Welcome to
Crowning Clock Tower, Batman.

620
00:48:40,588 --> 00:48:41,455
Nygma!

621
00:48:41,488 --> 00:48:42,791
What...

622
00:48:42,891 --> 00:48:44,324
What happened to you?

623
00:48:44,358 --> 00:48:48,897
Another riddle. But the answer
isn't one you're going to like.

624
00:48:57,705 --> 00:48:59,039
Hmm.

625
00:49:01,676 --> 00:49:04,344
I can't feel a thing.

626
00:49:08,048 --> 00:49:11,753
I can't feel... a thing.

627
00:49:11,820 --> 00:49:13,755
What did he do to me?

628
00:49:18,492 --> 00:49:19,561
The bomb!

629
00:49:19,594 --> 00:49:22,831
If I don't get out of here,
we're both going to die.

630
00:49:49,356 --> 00:49:52,694
Sergeant, take two men
and go down that alley.

631
00:49:56,263 --> 00:49:56,798
Nygma?

632
00:49:56,865 --> 00:49:59,433
He ran off. Fast, too.

633
00:49:59,466 --> 00:50:01,235
Looked like he was
hopped up on something.

634
00:50:01,301 --> 00:50:02,937
He couldn't have gotten far.

635
00:50:03,003 --> 00:50:04,873
Batman, are you okay?

636
00:50:04,906 --> 00:50:06,073
Why wouldn't I be?

637
00:50:06,106 --> 00:50:08,576
Look at you,
you look like hell.

638
00:50:08,977 --> 00:50:11,311
Besides...

639
00:50:12,847 --> 00:50:16,250
I'm getting reports...

640
00:50:16,283 --> 00:50:16,818
Of what?

641
00:50:16,885 --> 00:50:18,252
You're off your game.

642
00:50:18,285 --> 00:50:21,321
You're a little more
edgy than usual.

643
00:50:21,990 --> 00:50:22,824
I'm fine.

644
00:50:22,857 --> 00:50:24,291
Bullshit.

645
00:50:24,358 --> 00:50:27,060
We've worked with
each other for years.

646
00:50:27,529 --> 00:50:28,663
You're not fine.

647
00:50:30,832 --> 00:50:32,065
Look,

648
00:50:33,133 --> 00:50:36,336
if you ever need to talk,

649
00:50:38,338 --> 00:50:39,574
I'm here.

650
00:50:50,585 --> 00:50:53,821
Tell him it's delicious,
would you, Gino?

651
00:50:53,855 --> 00:50:55,823
Sure thing, boss. I can--

652
00:51:12,040 --> 00:51:15,108
You've got a lotta nerve,
bird boy.

653
00:51:17,045 --> 00:51:18,412
Is this supposed
to mean something?

654
00:51:18,445 --> 00:51:21,315
That's a piece of explosive
I found at Arkham.

655
00:51:21,348 --> 00:51:22,550
I think it belongs to you.

656
00:51:22,617 --> 00:51:25,720
That has nothing
to do with--

657
00:51:25,787 --> 00:51:26,955
Sure it does.

658
00:51:27,021 --> 00:51:29,089
Blow up Arkham,
let some crazies loose,

659
00:51:29,122 --> 00:51:30,959
keep everyone busy.

660
00:51:31,025 --> 00:51:32,225
But why?

661
00:51:32,259 --> 00:51:33,861
To pull off a heist?

662
00:51:33,928 --> 00:51:36,631
Kill a couple of
competing gangs?

663
00:51:36,664 --> 00:51:38,900
I told you that wasn't me.

664
00:51:38,967 --> 00:51:40,935
It was some other guy.

665
00:51:41,035 --> 00:51:42,135
What other guy?

666
00:51:42,202 --> 00:51:43,638
I don't know.

667
00:51:44,739 --> 00:51:45,940
Robin, is this--

668
00:51:46,007 --> 00:51:47,075
Watch and learn.

669
00:51:50,979 --> 00:51:52,513
Okay!

670
00:51:55,215 --> 00:51:57,585
Okay, I'll tell you
what I know.

671
00:51:57,685 --> 00:52:00,387
Last week, I got a call.

672
00:52:01,455 --> 00:52:03,323
<i>It was a dinner</i>
<i>for the five families.</i>

673
00:52:03,357 --> 00:52:05,627
<i>I thought it was</i>
<i>to discuss business,</i>

674
00:52:05,660 --> 00:52:06,761
<i>but as it turned out,</i>

675
00:52:06,828 --> 00:52:08,997
<i>it was just to get us all</i>
<i>in the same room.</i>

676
00:52:09,030 --> 00:52:10,698
I didn't call this.

677
00:52:10,765 --> 00:52:12,332
I thought you did, Vincent?

678
00:52:12,399 --> 00:52:14,902
Like I wanna
see your faces

679
00:52:15,003 --> 00:52:16,838
outside of Christmas Mass.

680
00:52:18,606 --> 00:52:20,642
<i>He stepped out of</i>
<i>the shadows so quick,</i>

681
00:52:20,708 --> 00:52:22,409
<i>we didn't even notice.</i>

682
00:52:22,910 --> 00:52:24,244
<i>He killed Vincent in a second,</i>

683
00:52:24,311 --> 00:52:26,114
<i>and then...</i>

684
00:52:26,146 --> 00:52:27,815
<i>Mayhem.</i>

685
00:52:46,567 --> 00:52:48,736
<i>He called himself "Bane."</i>

686
00:52:48,770 --> 00:52:51,471
<i>Asked me</i>
<i>where we held our explosives.</i>

687
00:52:51,506 --> 00:52:53,440
<i>Come on, what was I gonna do?</i>

688
00:52:53,473 --> 00:52:56,276
<i>I swear, I thought</i>
<i>I was gonna die.</i>

689
00:52:56,343 --> 00:52:58,211
<i>But he just looked at me...</i>

690
00:52:58,913 --> 00:53:01,916
<i>like I was... less.</i>

691
00:53:01,949 --> 00:53:03,751
<i>And then, he left.</i>

692
00:53:08,656 --> 00:53:11,224
And that's why you
beefed up your security.

693
00:53:11,291 --> 00:53:12,527
You're afraid he's coming back.

694
00:53:12,627 --> 00:53:16,496
Yeah, but instead,
I got you. Too bad.

695
00:53:18,733 --> 00:53:19,967
Move!

696
00:53:53,500 --> 00:53:56,537
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hey, hey! It's okay.

697
00:53:56,571 --> 00:53:57,237
You're okay.

698
00:53:57,270 --> 00:54:00,007
No. I can't be here.

699
00:54:00,641 --> 00:54:01,676
I can't!

700
00:54:04,746 --> 00:54:08,281
Just tell me what
you want and leave me alone.

701
00:54:08,315 --> 00:54:10,518
Where'd you say
you kept those explosives?

702
00:54:17,324 --> 00:54:18,693
Are you okay?

703
00:54:19,794 --> 00:54:21,095
No.

704
00:54:21,129 --> 00:54:22,196
What I did was...

705
00:54:22,262 --> 00:54:24,632
What you did is save us.

706
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:27,068
Batman was right.

707
00:54:27,101 --> 00:54:28,936
These skills
can be used for good.

708
00:54:28,970 --> 00:54:30,905
I didn't feel good, Robin.

709
00:54:31,239 --> 00:54:32,840
I felt...

710
00:54:32,907 --> 00:54:34,542
Out of control.

711
00:54:35,375 --> 00:54:37,377
I could've killed someone.

712
00:54:37,410 --> 00:54:39,147
But you didn't.

713
00:54:39,213 --> 00:54:41,783
The deprogramming is working,
Jean-Paul.

714
00:54:41,849 --> 00:54:43,383
Look how far you've come.

715
00:54:45,219 --> 00:54:47,320
Listen, I have to go
check out this lead.

716
00:54:47,354 --> 00:54:49,489
Head back to the cave,
and when I get back,

717
00:54:49,524 --> 00:54:51,793
we'll sort this out, okay?

718
00:55:28,262 --> 00:55:29,697
Bruce?

719
00:55:33,801 --> 00:55:35,435
I'm sorry, I...

720
00:55:35,468 --> 00:55:37,038
I didn't want to go home,
I thought--

721
00:55:37,104 --> 00:55:38,739
What happened?

722
00:55:39,140 --> 00:55:40,508
I was...

723
00:55:40,842 --> 00:55:41,876
mugged.

724
00:55:41,909 --> 00:55:43,544
You don't have to tell me
what happened,

725
00:55:43,644 --> 00:55:47,014
but don't insult me
by lying about it.

726
00:55:50,483 --> 00:55:52,854
Let me get something
for that wound.

727
00:55:53,486 --> 00:55:55,256
I shouldn't have come.

728
00:55:55,289 --> 00:55:57,091
I just need paper towels
and tape.

729
00:55:57,124 --> 00:55:59,060
And then I'll leave.

730
00:55:59,160 --> 00:56:00,962
-I'll pay for your time.
-What?

731
00:56:00,995 --> 00:56:03,264
I said, I shouldn't have come.

732
00:56:03,297 --> 00:56:04,298
I'm glad you did.

733
00:56:04,332 --> 00:56:06,634
When you called earlier...
Lie back.

734
00:56:07,134 --> 00:56:08,636
I was worried.

735
00:56:13,406 --> 00:56:16,277
This is bad.

736
00:56:16,310 --> 00:56:18,079
We should get you
to a hospital.

737
00:56:18,112 --> 00:56:20,248
No. No hospitals.

738
00:56:20,281 --> 00:56:21,349
Okay...

739
00:56:21,381 --> 00:56:23,885
Can I call someone? Alfred?

740
00:56:24,185 --> 00:56:25,019
No.

741
00:56:25,086 --> 00:56:26,921
He'll just make a fuss.

742
00:56:26,954 --> 00:56:30,291
You're lucky to have someone
in your life to make a fuss.

743
00:56:30,324 --> 00:56:32,226
This one is going
to need stitches.

744
00:56:32,260 --> 00:56:34,996
I have a bandage that will stop
the bleeding as best I can,

745
00:56:35,096 --> 00:56:36,264
but you need a doctor.

746
00:56:36,364 --> 00:56:38,933
Just sit back and relax.

747
00:56:44,005 --> 00:56:46,107
Here... Oh.

748
00:57:21,676 --> 00:57:23,544
It should be up ahead.

749
00:57:32,485 --> 00:57:34,655
Well, what do we have here?

750
00:57:34,722 --> 00:57:39,260
Please,
come in and find out.

751
00:58:04,318 --> 00:58:07,655
You can dispense
with the subterfuge, Mr. Drake.

752
00:58:08,122 --> 00:58:09,857
I know you're awake.

753
00:58:12,193 --> 00:58:14,528
You must be Bane.

754
00:58:14,562 --> 00:58:15,663
What do you want?

755
00:58:15,696 --> 00:58:19,066
You are the detective.
You tell me.

756
00:58:19,166 --> 00:58:21,035
What do I want?

757
00:58:28,009 --> 00:58:30,378
You killed four
of the five crime families,

758
00:58:30,411 --> 00:58:32,947
took their explosives,
destroyed Arkham.

759
00:58:33,681 --> 00:58:35,816
Well, go on.

760
00:58:37,818 --> 00:58:40,554
Maybe you're trying
to start a gang war.

761
00:58:40,621 --> 00:58:42,990
Or you were hired
by a rival mob.

762
00:58:43,024 --> 00:58:45,092
Nothing so mundane.

763
00:58:48,095 --> 00:58:50,031
Try again.

764
00:58:51,098 --> 00:58:52,900
You know who I am,

765
00:58:52,933 --> 00:58:56,070
- so you must know who--
- Yes.

766
00:58:56,103 --> 00:59:00,441
I know what Mr. Wayne likes
to play at during the night.

767
00:59:00,474 --> 00:59:03,411
It's a wonder that
more people don't know.

768
00:59:03,477 --> 00:59:07,181
He does such a poor job
covering it up.

769
00:59:07,815 --> 00:59:09,417
Him...

770
00:59:09,450 --> 00:59:10,851
You're here for him.

771
00:59:10,951 --> 00:59:12,186
Mmm-hmm.

772
00:59:12,720 --> 00:59:14,688
Arkham, the gangs...

773
00:59:14,755 --> 00:59:17,391
the police will be stretched
so thin that

774
00:59:17,458 --> 00:59:19,927
Batman will pick up the slack.

775
00:59:21,195 --> 00:59:23,030
And you knew that.

776
00:59:23,097 --> 00:59:26,600
You want him weak
so you can... what?

777
00:59:27,001 --> 00:59:28,102
Kill him?

778
00:59:28,135 --> 00:59:29,904
Break him.

779
00:59:29,937 --> 00:59:33,340
You are better at this
than I gave you credit for.

780
00:59:34,108 --> 00:59:34,909
But why?

781
00:59:34,975 --> 00:59:39,947
Bruce Wayne
has crippled this city.

782
00:59:39,980 --> 00:59:43,484
He has allowed
the weak to thrive.

783
00:59:43,552 --> 00:59:44,919
<i>His father knew that.</i>

784
00:59:44,985 --> 00:59:49,123
<i>His strength built this city</i>
<i>into the envy of the world.</i>

785
00:59:49,156 --> 00:59:53,627
<i>A dream that kept me going</i>
<i>for many years.</i>

786
00:59:53,694 --> 00:59:58,099
<i>So, imagine my surprise</i>
<i>when I arrived to find</i>

787
00:59:58,165 --> 00:59:59,133
<i>it has been turned into</i>

788
00:59:59,200 --> 01:00:01,235
<i>-a cesspool of weakness...</i>
-Come back!

789
01:00:01,302 --> 01:00:03,037
-Hey! Aren't you gonna help me?
<i>-...and charity.</i>

790
01:00:03,070 --> 01:00:05,005
<i>I wonder how Bruce's father</i>
<i>would feel</i>

791
01:00:05,072 --> 01:00:07,576
<i>knowing that his son</i>
<i>is the reason...</i>

792
01:00:07,608 --> 01:00:08,876
<i>...it has become a city</i>

793
01:00:08,943 --> 01:00:12,480
<i>of weaklings, vagrants,</i>
<i>and madmen.</i>

794
01:00:12,514 --> 01:00:15,983
<i>I've come to fix this city.</i>

795
01:00:16,050 --> 01:00:22,857
The weak will perish
and the strong will thrive.

796
01:00:22,957 --> 01:00:28,597
When Batman finds you
lifeless like the last Robin,

797
01:00:28,629 --> 01:00:31,966
his spirit will
finally be broken.

798
01:00:32,032 --> 01:00:35,336
And I can get rid of the thing
that is holding Gotham back

799
01:00:35,402 --> 01:00:38,038
from its return to greatness.

800
01:00:50,718 --> 01:00:53,654
So you're crazy,
just like the rest of them.

801
01:01:03,831 --> 01:01:05,132
Oh, I think you'll find

802
01:01:05,166 --> 01:01:08,435
I am nothing
like the rest of them.

803
01:02:38,926 --> 01:02:42,463
Father, forgive me.

804
01:02:44,031 --> 01:02:45,533
I...

805
01:02:46,000 --> 01:02:47,801
Tonight I remembered...

806
01:02:49,503 --> 01:02:51,005
all of it. I...

807
01:02:51,573 --> 01:02:53,173
I saw what I did.

808
01:02:53,742 --> 01:02:57,444
And it was... horrible.

809
01:02:59,079 --> 01:03:02,149
How can I live knowing that...

810
01:03:02,182 --> 01:03:04,318
that there's something
inside of me

811
01:03:04,385 --> 01:03:06,220
that can do such harm?

812
01:03:07,488 --> 01:03:08,723
My son,

813
01:03:08,757 --> 01:03:13,394
the Lord can take what is meant
for evil and turn it to good.

814
01:03:13,427 --> 01:03:17,498
What is inside of you
is meant for something more.

815
01:03:18,365 --> 01:03:19,967
Your experience, skills,

816
01:03:20,034 --> 01:03:22,604
God can use those
to help the world

817
01:03:22,671 --> 01:03:24,606
instead of hurting it.

818
01:03:24,639 --> 01:03:28,142
-How?
-By accepting your destiny.

819
01:03:28,175 --> 01:03:32,681
By becoming the knight
Saint Dumas wants you to be.

820
01:03:58,439 --> 01:04:00,575
You are chosen.

821
01:04:00,608 --> 01:04:02,109
Accept your destiny

822
01:04:02,176 --> 01:04:05,780
and become that
which you are meant to be!

823
01:04:05,814 --> 01:04:07,481
Azrael!

824
01:04:34,441 --> 01:04:35,376
Alfred?

825
01:04:35,409 --> 01:04:37,712
<i>Master Bruce,</i>
<i>it's Tim.</i>

826
01:04:37,812 --> 01:04:39,179
<i>He's been hurt.</i>

827
01:04:52,426 --> 01:04:53,927
Huh?

828
01:04:54,796 --> 01:04:56,029
Hmm.

829
01:05:06,608 --> 01:05:07,509
What happened?

830
01:05:07,542 --> 01:05:10,043
I figured it out, Bruce,
who blew up Arkham.

831
01:05:10,077 --> 01:05:11,345
Where's Jean-Paul?

832
01:05:11,378 --> 01:05:12,479
He got spooked.

833
01:05:12,547 --> 01:05:13,782
You should've seen him though.

834
01:05:13,882 --> 01:05:15,683
He moved like lightning.

835
01:05:15,750 --> 01:05:17,117
I think the system is triggered

836
01:05:17,184 --> 01:05:18,952
in a life or death type
of scenario.

837
01:05:18,986 --> 01:05:20,855
He took out half a dozen
of Bertinelli's men

838
01:05:20,954 --> 01:05:22,791
in a couple of seconds.
It was crazy.

839
01:05:22,824 --> 01:05:25,492
-What were you thinking?
-Master Bruce! I--

840
01:05:25,527 --> 01:05:27,394
No. No, Alfred.

841
01:05:27,494 --> 01:05:29,129
I told you to stay here.

842
01:05:29,196 --> 01:05:30,397
Actually, you didn't.

843
01:05:30,431 --> 01:05:32,700
-Your exact words--
-You knew what I meant!

844
01:05:32,734 --> 01:05:34,067
You're not ready.

845
01:05:34,101 --> 01:05:35,369
You could have gotten killed.

846
01:05:35,436 --> 01:05:36,538
But I didn't.

847
01:05:36,571 --> 01:05:39,473
And I found out who's creating
all this chaos in Gotham.

848
01:05:39,541 --> 01:05:43,043
-They call him Bane, and--
-You're fired.

849
01:05:43,645 --> 01:05:45,112
-What?
-Master Bruce.

850
01:05:45,179 --> 01:05:47,549
Please,
let me get you some food.

851
01:05:47,582 --> 01:05:51,084
No. I need a partner
that does what he's told.

852
01:05:51,118 --> 01:05:53,387
I can't have another Robin die

853
01:05:53,420 --> 01:05:55,255
because they don't
follow orders.

854
01:05:55,322 --> 01:05:56,524
I'm not Jason.

855
01:05:56,558 --> 01:05:58,660
No. You're not.

856
01:05:59,226 --> 01:06:01,061
Get your things and leave.

857
01:06:01,128 --> 01:06:03,531
Alfred will drive you home.

858
01:06:06,200 --> 01:06:08,135
I'll have a talk with him.

859
01:06:08,168 --> 01:06:11,673
He's just tired.
He'll come around.

860
01:06:11,773 --> 01:06:13,240
I don't think so.

861
01:06:53,247 --> 01:06:56,718
Alfred, Tim, I'm tired
and I shouldn't have said--

862
01:07:28,550 --> 01:07:29,817
Alfred! Tim!

863
01:07:45,867 --> 01:07:47,334
Bane.

864
01:07:48,402 --> 01:07:54,008
I have sought you out,
Batman.

865
01:07:54,074 --> 01:07:56,911
The son of Thomas Wayne,

866
01:07:56,945 --> 01:08:01,516
a boy of privilege,
a boy of tragedy.

867
01:08:01,549 --> 01:08:04,184
You are the weakness
that drowns this city

868
01:08:04,217 --> 01:08:06,253
and I intend to break you.

869
01:08:13,861 --> 01:08:15,797
Then give it your best shot.

870
01:08:16,631 --> 01:08:18,365
Good.

871
01:08:51,566 --> 01:08:54,969
They say you are
the greatest detective.

872
01:08:56,104 --> 01:08:59,172
And yet you did not
see this coming.

873
01:09:14,555 --> 01:09:18,693
You are a crutch
this city relies upon.

874
01:09:18,726 --> 01:09:23,463
But now it's time that they
stood on their own two feet.

875
01:09:42,116 --> 01:09:44,184
Yes...

876
01:09:44,217 --> 01:09:48,956
Yes. I know you want to hide.

877
01:09:49,023 --> 01:09:51,693
You are always hiding.

878
01:09:51,726 --> 01:09:53,293
From the world...

879
01:09:53,360 --> 01:09:55,195
from the people close to you.

880
01:09:55,228 --> 01:09:59,133
Hiding from your own failure.

881
01:09:59,167 --> 01:10:03,470
But you cannot hide
from destiny.

882
01:10:04,739 --> 01:10:06,741
From me.

883
01:10:50,151 --> 01:10:53,888
I have dreamt of you, Bruce.

884
01:10:53,955 --> 01:10:56,958
Oh, I've dreamt of your family.

885
01:10:58,226 --> 01:11:00,128
Of the strength
your father must have had

886
01:11:00,161 --> 01:11:02,697
to build his empire.

887
01:11:04,766 --> 01:11:07,400
An empire
you are not fit to rule

888
01:11:07,434 --> 01:11:10,037
because you lack the strength.

889
01:11:12,073 --> 01:11:15,543
The strength to save Tim.

890
01:11:16,778 --> 01:11:18,045
Alfred.

891
01:11:19,580 --> 01:11:20,915
The city.

892
01:11:22,683 --> 01:11:23,985
Jason.

893
01:11:28,823 --> 01:11:30,091
Jason?

894
01:11:30,158 --> 01:11:34,729
The strength
to save your parents.

895
01:11:34,762 --> 01:11:38,199
Oh, how you
let them die, Bruce,

896
01:11:38,298 --> 01:11:39,700
while you sat in an alley,

897
01:11:39,767 --> 01:11:45,239
mewling like a calf
as your parents bled

898
01:11:45,273 --> 01:11:48,643
and their murderer
disappeared into the night.

899
01:11:48,709 --> 01:11:51,512
Oh, you must be glad
they aren't alive

900
01:11:51,546 --> 01:11:53,581
to see what you've become,

901
01:11:53,648 --> 01:11:58,451
to see what you've
allowed Gotham to become.

902
01:11:59,954 --> 01:12:01,989
Enough with your toys!

903
01:12:02,056 --> 01:12:03,624
Face me with your fists!

904
01:12:14,367 --> 01:12:16,304
Beg for mercy!

905
01:12:16,336 --> 01:12:18,639
Scream my name!

906
01:12:19,674 --> 01:12:21,676
Go to hell.

907
01:12:21,709 --> 01:12:25,112
I am Bane.

908
01:12:25,146 --> 01:12:26,379
I could kill you,

909
01:12:26,413 --> 01:12:29,382
but death
would only end your agony

910
01:12:29,449 --> 01:12:32,520
and silence your shame.

911
01:12:32,587 --> 01:12:36,456
Instead, I will simply...

912
01:12:47,668 --> 01:12:49,036
Break you.

913
01:13:15,162 --> 01:13:16,163
What happened?

914
01:13:16,230 --> 01:13:17,565
Explosion of some kind.

915
01:13:17,632 --> 01:13:18,633
Everyone is evacuated

916
01:13:18,666 --> 01:13:20,768
and Fire is on the way.

917
01:13:21,602 --> 01:13:24,338
Of course, the press
is having a field day.

918
01:13:24,404 --> 01:13:27,108
I think every station
in town is here.

919
01:13:33,381 --> 01:13:34,682
Any luck?

920
01:13:35,216 --> 01:13:36,150
No.

921
01:13:36,183 --> 01:13:37,852
He's not answering.

922
01:13:37,919 --> 01:13:39,186
I should go.

923
01:13:39,220 --> 01:13:40,521
Bruce...

924
01:13:48,596 --> 01:13:51,966
Get one of those floodlights
on the second story roof!

925
01:13:59,273 --> 01:14:01,375
Who the hell is this guy?

926
01:14:01,441 --> 01:14:03,044
Now, Gotham,

927
01:14:03,077 --> 01:14:06,881
<i>you must do what you</i>
<i>haven't done for a generation.</i>

928
01:14:08,481 --> 01:14:10,117
Fend for yourself!

929
01:14:10,151 --> 01:14:11,619
Batman?

930
01:14:32,173 --> 01:14:33,207
Take him out!

931
01:14:54,795 --> 01:14:57,298
That can't...
that can't be Batman, can it?

932
01:14:57,365 --> 01:14:58,766
What's going to happen
to the city?

933
01:14:58,799 --> 01:15:01,135
Get back! Everyone, get back!

934
01:15:01,168 --> 01:15:02,536
Move!

935
01:15:05,272 --> 01:15:06,807
Good God.

936
01:15:06,841 --> 01:15:10,311
This place is about
to become hell on earth.
